Release the Perl dist Skilletor (perl/) as 0.002. The release itself waits for the maintainer's explicit go.

State on 2026-11-16: 0.001 was released with dzil on 2026-10-24. The tag 0.001 is on origin and perl/Changes carries its version line. Whether the upload reached CPAN has not been checked from here. 31 commits under perl/ have landed since, and perl/Changes {{$NEXT}} is long.

Blocker: perl/cpanfile now requires Text::Nunjucks 0.001, which was never released (p5-text-nunjucks has no tags). Skilletor 0.001 had no such dependency. A 0.002 on CPAN cannot install until Text::Nunjucks is there (see the needs link).

Before the release:
- Confirm that 0.001 is on CPAN.
- Run the skilletor-release-manager pre-release audit of perl/: {{$NEXT}} written as one consumer-facing document, the cpanfile, and the tarball contents per gather_exclude_match in dist.ini.
- Get a green `prove -lr t` against the released Text::Nunjucks rather than the checkout on PERL5LIB.

Rewritten 2026-11-18: superseded as "0.002 from perl/" by the ACK package work (k242). The dist is at the root now and the next release is 0.008 (= plugin 0.8.0). Text::Nunjucks 0.001 is on CPAN since 2026-11-17, so the needs link is gone. The release is still the maintainer's gate.

Before the release:
- ack-paket merged into main (the hub merges; no session pushes main).
- The binaries probe green on all four legs, bundle workflow pinned by commit (k242).
- Release machine: Dist::Zilla::PluginBundle::Author::GETTY 0.328 or later, PAR::Packer, the dist's deps from CPAN.
- skilletor-release-manager pre-release audit; the Changes section for 0.008 is written for users.

Release: docs/release.md steps 1-6 -- dzil release on a clean main; binaries.yml runs on release: published; check SHA256SUMS; commit bin/skilletor-binaries.sha256 from it (k191's gate); marketplace license MIT -> Artistic-2.0.

